/.claude
/.scratch
/node_modules
/dist
*.tgz

# A `.env` at any depth, and any variant of it, holds a real key. The `.env.example` files
# committed beside them hold none, and are the one name let back in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# What an example under `examples/` writes: its own dependency tree and the lockfile that
# comes with it (each is a real npm application that installs the published package with
# `npm install`, and a committed lockfile is what 1.0.0 buys), and the Workspace, agent
# directory and Sessions its Agent Instance writes. The committed `settings.json` beside them
# is not these.
#
# These three lines also decide what Biome sees, because `biome.json` sets `vcs.useIgnoreFile`.
# That is the whole of what keeps four dependency trees out of `biome check .`, and no Biome
# configuration names `examples/` at all. Each example's own sources stay linted, which is
# wanted.
/examples/*/node_modules
/examples/*/package-lock.json
/examples/*/state

# The documentation site's own dependency tree, which carries a second TypeScript and is
# installed by `npm run docs:dev`, `npm run docs:build` and `npm run check:docs` alone, never
# by `npm ci` at the root (`site/README.md`).
/site/node_modules
/site/.vitepress/cache
/site/.vitepress/dist

# The generated reference, in full, sidebar included. It was committed so that a change to the
# public API arrived as a readable diff; a signature block is HTML now, and a diff over `<span>`s
# and `<a href>`s does not do that. What that costs a reviewer is argued in `CLAUDE.md`.
# `npm run check:docs` regenerates it and asserts that every page still has a linked signature
# block on it. This line also decides what Biome sees, because `biome.json` sets
# `vcs.useIgnoreFile`: the sidebar TypeDoc writes here is one minified line of JSON, and it used
# to need a rule of its own to keep it out of `npm run lint`. A directory nobody commits needs no
# exception inside it.
/site/reference
